'''Formicidaean Ariant''' (超爆獣アリアント, ''Chō Bakujū Arianto'', '''Super Explosive Beast Ariant''') is a [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemy that appears in [[Legend Stages]] and [[Cats of the Cosmos]]'s [[Zombie Outbreaks]]. It was added in [[Version 11.8 Update|Version 11.8]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Formicidaean Ariant
|image = E 614.png
|money drop = 280¢ - 1,106¢
|first appearance=[[Ashvini Desert]]<br>[[Jinfore Volcano]]<br>'''UL''': [[Ape Lord's Revenge|Sub-chapter 48 - Ape Lord's Revenge]]<br>'''CotC''': [[Catseye Nebula (Cats of the Cosmos)/Outbreak|Chapter 2 - Catseye Nebula Outbreak]]|latest appearance='''ZL''': [[Beast of Monte Cristo|Sub-chapter 7 - Beast of Monte Cristo]]}}

==Enemy==
Formicidaean Ariant steadily inches towards the [[Cat Base]] with its swollen abdomen. After a short burrow, it turns its rear towards the first cat it reaches and waits for its abdomen to further swell up like a balloon until it pops, dealing an enormous amount of damage three times in quick succession; this attack covers a wider area on each hit, reaching -390~390 on the third. Once it blows up, its abdomen immediately regrows, yet it still has to wait for some time before it can attack again. Like most Behemoths, it's also immune to certain effects, including [[Immune to Freeze|Freeze]], [[Immune to Weaken|Weaken]] and [[Immune to Knockback|Knockback]].

==Strategy==
At 200% strength magnification, any unit caught in Formicidaean Ariant's blast will suffer 90,000 damage just for one hit; the damage adds up to a maximum of 270,000, meaning most units—let alone the Cat Base—can't even withstand one abdominal assault from this miscre''ant''.  Its weakness lies in its relatively short standing range, long foreswing, vulnerability to the default [[Cat Cannon]]/[[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] and a typing that can easily be exploited by strong [[:Category:Behemoth Slayer Cats|Behemoth Slayer units]] or disposable [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombies]], allowing it to be killed without ever causing trouble. [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] is particularly effective in that it has both Behemoth Slayer and Massive Damage against Zombies, as well as Soulstrike if Ariant wasn't finished off. This unit preys on a lack of const''ant'' DPS flow to your front lines, so as long as you keep a steady line of units such as [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCats]], you can ''ant''icipate an easy fight.

It should also be noted that, since Ariant has very short standing range and is still susceptible to Slow, [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] or other similar ''ant''i-Zombie units can keep it from burrowing, giving time for your attackers to finish it off at low risk.

