==Trivia==
*[[wikipedia:Formicidae|Formicidae]] is the family of insects that contains all ants, and ''ari'' (蟻) is the Japanese word for ant, so "Formicidaean Ari-ant" means "Ant-ant of the Ant Family".
*The name Ariant is one letter away from Aiant, the Japanese name of the ant Pokémon [[bulbapedia:Durant (Pokémon)|Durant]].
*Its description is a reference to one of Aesop's Fables, [[wikipedia:The Ant and the Grasshopper|The Ant and the Grasshopper]], which involves an ant who works hard to stockpile food for winter.
*It is specifically based on a [[wikipedia:Honeypot ant|honeypot ant]], which have specialized workers called repletes that get gorged with food enough for their abdomens to swell up like Formicidaean Ariant's.
**Although Ariant's gender isn't stated, worker ants are female in real life.
*Its exploding abdomen could be inspired by ''[[wikipedia:Colobopsis saundersi|Colobopsis saundersi]]'', a species of ant that can rupture its gaster as a defence mechanism.
*Its Zombie trait may be an indirect reference to [[wikipedia:Ophiocordyceps unilateralis|''Ophiocordyceps unilateralis'']] (zombie-ant fungus) and its [https://youtu.be/vijGdWn5-h8 hosts].
*Since [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]] generally reference ''Monster Hunter'', Formicidaean Ariant is likely intended to parallel [[wikia:monsterhunter:Altaroth|Altaroth]], insectoid monsters with the abdomen-swelling characteristic shared by honeypot ants and Ariant. Moreover, Altaroth is regarded as one of the weakest monsters in the series, and Ariant has the second-lowest health of all Behemoths.
*Unlike real ants, Formicidaean Ariant has no mandibles and four limbs instead of six; though, as a decomposing corpse, it's possible that they already rotted away.
*Although its description says its stomach explodes, Ariant lacks the [[Explosion]] ability, as Ariant was added first.
*The pattern on its abdomen looks somewhat like a screaming face with two eyes, two small nostrils, and a mouth gaping wide open.
*It has the longest revive time out of any Zombie.

